According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the Global Security Orchestration, Automation and Response (SOAR) Market was valued at approximately USD 1.63 billion in 2025 and is estimated to reach USD 1.90 billion in 2026. The market is projected to grow to USD 6.45 billion by 2034, registering a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 16.5% during the 2026–2034 forecast period. Rising cybersecurity workloads, increasing incident-response complexity, and the need to coordinate security tools are driving demand for SOAR platforms.
SOAR solutions help security teams connect security technologies, automate repetitive processes, organize incident workflows, and coordinate responses to threats. By using playbooks and integrations with systems such as security information and event management platforms, endpoint security tools, and threat intelligence feeds, SOAR technology can help security operations centers standardize investigation and response activities.
